   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI_03">Reinhardstrasse 7</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name> VIII</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>(<name type="geo" key="G_CHE">Switzerland</name>)</addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Miss <name type="person" key="weav76">Weaver</name>
                        </salute>
                    </opener>
                    <p>Thanks for your letter and for the copy of <name type="work" key="THE_EGOIST">
                            <hi rend="underline">The</hi> <hi rend="underline">Egoist</hi>
                        </name> (<date when="1915-09-01">1 September</date>). You are very kind to offer to send me copies of your paper. I shall be very glad to receive them and shall avail myself of your kindness at least during <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">my forced residence</seg> here. I shall also beg you to accept from me a copy of <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="work" key="A_PORTRAIT">the book</rs>
                        </seg> when (and if) it is published.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1915-09-14">14 September 1915</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">JJ sought refuge in Zurich at the end of June 1915, leaving Trieste after Italy entered the war.</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">
                    <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>, which Harriet Weaver was publishing serially in <name type="work" key="W_THEEGOIST">The Egoist</name>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
